Contract: explore every reachable terminal observation.
Both allowed initial envelopes carry node 3. The first payload is approved, the second is declined. The shared key returns only the node.
On advance, the machine carries the payload unchanged to node 4. At node 4, flush returns that payload's approval status.
The explorer queues only the first envelope per node key, expands it, and returns the set of terminal observations.
